  "notes": "USAGE:\n{強|つよ}がる follows the common ～がる pattern, which turns an adjective into a verb meaning \"to show signs of\" or \"to act as if.\" Here, {強|つよ}い (strong) becomes {強|つよ}がる (to act strong). The implication is always that the toughness is a front.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nConjugation: {強|つよ}がらない (negative), {強|つよ}がって (te-form), {強|つよ}がった (past). Godan verb ending in る (ら{行|ぎょう}).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {強|つよ}がって{見|み}せる (to put on a show of being tough)\n- {強|つよ}がらなくていい (you don't need to act tough)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{意地|いじ}を{張|は}る means to be stubborn or headstrong, while {強|つよ}がる specifically emphasizes hiding vulnerability behind a brave front.",
